  "worked_solution": "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ is continuous over the entire interval $[0,\\pi ],$ but the function $\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x$ is not defined at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ],$ namely\n\n$$\n[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\cup (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
